10090295|t|Acute renal failure induced by cisplatin chemotherapy in ovarian cancer patients.
10090295|a|Cisplatin is an effective chemotherapeutic agent for ovarian neoplasms, but its therapeutic potential is compromised by nephrotoxicity. We examined patients who developed acute renal failure following intravenous cisplatin administration. Elevated serum creatinine, severe proteinuria, and metabolic acidosis were observed within 7 days. The findings confirm that cisplatin induces acute renal failure and metabolic acidosis during therapeutic regimens.
