10372223|t|Bleomycin-induced pulmonary fibrosis in experimental mouse models.
10372223|a|Bleomycin is frequently used in chemotherapy, but clinical utility is severely limited by pulmonary toxicity. Intratracheal administration of bleomycin in mice produced widespread alveolar inflammation and severe pulmonary fibrosis. Extensive collagen deposition, lung stiffness, and respiratory distress were documented. Bleomycin is confirmed as a causative agent of severe pulmonary fibrosis and alveolar inflammation in animal models.
